  "rationales": {"U":"'easy (nearly automatic) inclusion' is subjective and lacks measurable criteria; users may disagree on what constitutes 'easy' or 'nearly automatic', impairing shared understanding","A":"'nearly automatic' is inherently ambiguous—it admits infinite interpretations (e.g., one-click vs. zero-configuration vs. <5s latency) and conflicts with 'facilities for' which dilutes agent responsibility","C":"The requirement to 'be maintained under a version control system' is broadly correct for modern software practice, though unspecified VCS type or compliance scope (e.g., all source, configs, scripts?) leaves minor correctness risk","V":"No testable pass/fail criterion exists: 'easy (nearly automatic) inclusion' cannot be objectively verified; no observable behavior, timing threshold, success metric, or integration artifact is defined"},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace subjective phrasing with objective, user-actionable criteria","A":"Specify exact integration mechanism, trigger condition, and success indicator; eliminate approximators like 'nearly'","C":"Keep unchanged but consider adding scope clarification in future refinement","V":"Define verifiable acceptance criteria: e.g., 'The build pipeline shall generate a valid Gemini environment manifest file within 30 seconds of Git tag push, without manual intervention'"},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"easy (nearly automatic) inclusion","rewrite":"shall support inclusion into the Gemini software environment via automated CI/CD pipeline triggered by Git tag push"},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"nearly automatic","rewrite":"fully automated, requiring zero manual steps after source code commit and tag creation"},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"must include facilities for easy (nearly automatic) inclusion into the Gemini software environment","rewrite":"shall produce a deployable Gemini environment package (format: OCI image) within 30 seconds of receiving a signed Git tag event from the primary repository"}
  ]
}
